{"model": "qwen3.8-27b", "qid": 11606, "category": "engineering", "gold": "C", "answer": "C", "conf": 95, "raw": "\n\nUsing the approximate series equivalent circuit (neglecting magnetizing branch), the plugging slip varies from\n\n\\[\ns_i = 1+\\frac{960}{1000}=1.96\n\\]\n\nto\n\n\\[\ns_f = 1\n\\]\n\nat standstill.\n\nSynchronous speed:\n\n\\[\nn_s=\\frac{120f}{P}=\\frac{120(50)}{6}=1000\\text{ rpm}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\omega_s=\\frac{2\\pi(1000)}{60}=104.72\\text{ rad/s}\n\\]\n\nFor a star-connected motor,\n\n\\[\nV_{ph}=\\frac{420}{\\sqrt{3}},\\qquad 3V_{ph}^2=420^2=176400\n\\]\n\nThe braking torque magnitude is\n\n\\[\nT(s)=\\frac{3V_{ph}^2 R_2'/s}{\\omega_s\\left[(R_1+R_2'/s)^2+(X_1+X_2')^2\\right]}\n\\]\n\nwith\n\n\\[\nR_1=R_2'=1.0\\ \\Omega,\\qquad X_1+X_2'=4.0\\ \\Omega\n\\]\n\nThe plugging time is\n\n\\[\nt=\\int_{1}^{1.96}\\frac{J\\omega_s\\,ds}{T(s)}\n\\]\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n\\[\nt=\\frac{J\\omega_s^2}{3V_{ph}^2R_2'}\n\\int_1^{1.96}\n\\left[s(R_1^2+X^2)+2R_1R_2'+\\frac{R_2'^2}{s}\\right]ds\n\\]\n\nSubstituting values:\n\n\\[\nt \\approx 4.99\\text{ s}\n\\]\n\nSo the closest option is **5.0 s**.\n\nANSWER: C\nCONFIDENCE: 95", "correct0": true}
